# Day 48 - Build The Verdict Engine

## 60 Days Claude AI Challenge

Today, I built **The Verdict Engine**, an AI-powered decision-support application designed to help users make better decisions using grounded research and weighted scoring.

## What I Learned

- **Grounded Research:** Using real and citable sources instead of fabricated data.
- **Weighted Decision Scoring:** Allowing users to assign priority weights to different criteria and dynamically update rankings.
- **Transparency by Design:** Clearly presenting sources, estimates, and resolved conflicts.
- **Decision-Support UX:** Building a responsive and user-friendly interface for comparing real-world options.

## Key Features

- AI-powered research and comparison
- Adjustable criteria weights
- Live ranking updates
- Source transparency
- Conflict resolution insights
- Interactive decision-support interface

## Tools Used

- Claude AI
- HTML
- CSS
- JavaScript
- GitHub

## Key Takeaway

This challenge helped me understand how AI can be used to build transparent decision-support systems that combine real research, user priorities, and weighted scoring to make complex decisions easier.

